// Title: Sysinternals PsSuspend Suspicious Execution
// Sigma ID: 4beb6ae0-f85b-41e2-8f18-8668abc8af78
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-03-23 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects suspicious execution of Sysinternals PsSuspend, where the utility is used to suspend
//   critical processes such as AV or EDR to bypass defenses
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/pssuspend
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1638069413717975046
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_pssuspend_susp_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "pssuspend.exe" or (FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pssuspend64a.exe")) and ProcessCommandLine contains "msmpeng.exe"
